# The Mellon Fellowships in the Humanities: Protecting an Endangered Species.

**Authors:** Hoopes, Judith

## Abstract
The Andrew W. Mellon Foundation combined its concern that few top flight scholars are choosing the humanities for careers and its awareness of the current oversupply of humanities faculty to create a $24 million fellowship program to direct talented graduate students into English and comparative literature, American studies, history, classics, archaeology, linguistics, philosophy, art history, religion, and musicology. (MSE)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ271394

